  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Bilirubin:</strong>&nbsp;Elevated levels may indicate liver dysfunction, hemolysis, or bile duct obstruction.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>ALT (SGPT) and AST (SGOT):</strong>&nbsp;Elevated in hepatocellular injury (e.g., hepatitis, liver toxicity)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>ALP:</strong>&nbsp;Raised levels may suggest cholestasis, bile duct obstruction, or bone disease.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>GGT:</strong>&nbsp;Elevated in liver disease, especially alcoholic liver disease and bile duct obstruction.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Albumin:</strong>&nbsp;Decreased levels may reflect impaired liver synthetic function.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Total Protein and A/G Ratio:</strong> Helps assess liver synthetic ability and differential diagnosis between liver or other systemic diseases.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
